<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">partners</span>
    <h1 class="page-h1">Refer a client, earn 20% for a year.</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      Send us a company that buys Prospektor and you get 20% of what it pays us, every month, for its first twelve months.
      Run workspaces for your own clients and they are 20% off instead.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pricing-faq">
  <div class="pricing-faq-inner">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <dl class="pricing-faq-list">
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>1. Get your link</dt>
        <dd>
          {%- if rewardful.signup %}
          Sign up as a partner and you get a link of your own. Rewardful runs the programme for us: your link, your clicks and your balance are all there.
          {%- else %}
          Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we send you your link. Rewardful runs the programme for us: your link, your clicks and your balance are all there.
          {%- endif %}
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>2. Send it to a client</dt>
        <dd>They buy Prospektor through your link, by the month or the year up front. The first partner link a buyer used is the one that counts, and a workspace has one partner.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>3. Get paid</dt>
        <dd>You earn 20% of every invoice they pay for twelve months. Each line becomes payable thirty days after its invoice is paid, which is past the money-back window, and Rewardful pays it out.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-faq-item">
        <dt>Running Prospektor for your own clients?</dt>
        <dd>An agency that pays for the workspaces it runs for its clients gets 20% off each one instead. A workspace only ever earns one of the two: the discount, or the share.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="legal-inner">
    <h2 class="section-h2">The terms</h2>
    <ol class="partner-terms">
      <li>You cannot refer yourself: not your own domain, your own workspace, your own card, or an address at your company.</li>
      <li>A company that has ever had a workspace cannot be referred. Deleted counts as ever.</li>
      <li>The first partner link a buyer used is the one that counts. One partner per workspace.</li>
      <li>A workspace you pay for at 20% off does not also earn 20% back.</li>
      <li>No ads on our name, and no coupon sites.</li>
      <li>We can end a partnership and cancel unpaid earnings if the rules are broken.</li>
      <li>Earnings become payable thirty days after the invoice they come from is paid, and are paid out through Rewardful.</li>
    </ol>
    {%- if rewardful.signup %}
    <p><a class="btn-cta" href="{{ rewardful.signup }}" rel="noopener">Sign up as a partner</a></p>
    {%- else %}
    <p>Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we send you your link.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="partner-note">Your link and your balance are in Rewardful, which runs the programme for us. What its cookie records, and how to switch it off, is in <a href="/privacy/#cookies">the privacy notice</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
